  "Number": 13,
  "Question": "\\(R\\) varies directly as \\(S\\) and inversely as \\(T.\\) When \\(R=\\dfrac43\\) and \\(T=\\dfrac9{14},\\) \\(S=\\dfrac37.\\) Find \\(S\\) when \\(R=\\sqrt{48}\\) and \\(T=\\sqrt{75}.\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(28\\)",
    "B": "\\(30\\)",
    "C": "\\(40\\)",
    "D": "\\(42\\)",
    "E": "\\(60\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "Direct variation with \\(S\\) puts \\(S\\) in the numerator, while inverse variation with \\(T\\) puts \\(T\\) in the denominator. Thus, for \\(T\\ne0\\),\n\\[\nR=k\\frac ST,\n\\]\nwhere \\(k\\) is constant. The initial values give\n\\[\nk=\\frac{RT}{S}\n=\\frac{\\left(\\frac43\\right)\\left(\\frac9{14}\\right)}{\\frac37}\n=2.\n\\]\nTherefore \\(S=RT/2\\). Both new radicands are positive, so\n\\[\nS=\\frac{\\sqrt{48}\\sqrt{75}}2\n=\\frac{\\sqrt{3600}}2\n=\\boxed{30},\n\\]\nwhich is choice B.",
